# Mermaid Diagram Readability

When generating Mermaid diagrams, always use thick, high-contrast lines so they remain readable in Cursor chat.

## Required styling

1. Start every diagram with a `%%{init: ...}%%` block that sets `stroke-width: 3px` via `themeCSS`.
2. Use dark stroke colors (`#1a1a1a`) for contrast.
3. Prefer `==>` over `-->` for flowchart arrows.
4. Add `linkStyle default stroke-width:3px,stroke:#1a1a1a` on flowcharts.

## Flowchart init block

```text
%%{init: {'theme':'base', 'themeVariables': {'lineColor':'#1a1a1a'}, 'themeCSS': '.flowchart-link, .edgePath .path, path.flowchart-link { stroke-width: 3px !important; stroke: #1a1a1a !important; } .arrowheadPath { fill: #1a1a1a !important; stroke: #1a1a1a !important; }'}}%%
```

## Sequence diagram init block

```text
%%{init: {'theme':'base', 'themeVariables': {'signalColor':'#1a1a1a'}, 'themeCSS': '.messageLine0, .messageLine1, .loopLine { stroke-width: 3px !important; stroke: #1a1a1a !important; } .arrowheadPath { fill: #1a1a1a !important; }'}}%%
```

## Example

```mermaid
%%{init: {'theme':'base', 'themeVariables': {'lineColor':'#1a1a1a'}, 'themeCSS': '.flowchart-link, .edgePath .path { stroke-width: 3px !important; stroke: #1a1a1a !important; } .arrowheadPath { fill: #1a1a1a !important; }'}}%%
flowchart LR
    A ==> B
    B ==> C
    linkStyle default stroke-width:3px,stroke:#1a1a1a
```
